(b) Proof that a person performed any of the acts set forth in this section or proof that a person knowingly received the benefits of such acts or proof that any of the acts specified in this section were done on the premises in possession of a person with that person's knowledge shall be prima facie evidence that such person is responsible for such prohibited acts.
(Code 2011, § 60-1; Ord. No. 96-2, § I, 2-6-1996)
State Law reference— Damaging, injuring or interfering with property of public utility companies, municipalities or political subdivisions, O.C.G.A. § 16-7-25.

